      ":question/problem": "In a gas station, $55%$ of the customers buy regular gasoline while $45%$ buy premium gasoline. If $60%$ of the customers that buy regular gasoline usually pay with a credit card and the probability that a randomly selected customer pays with a credit card is $0.645,$ what is the probability that a randomly selected customer who buys premium gasoline usually pays with a credit card? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places."
